---
import ContactIcon from '../components/ContactIcon.astro';
import '../styles/utility-approved.css';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy and site information" cta={false}>
 <article class="ut-reading ut-policy-layout rd-wrap rd-page">
 <header class="rd-pagehead"><h1>Privacy and site information</h1><p>How this site handles your inquiry draft and what the product information covers.</p></header>
 <div class="ut-policy-columns"><nav class="ut-toc" aria-label="Privacy topics"><a href="#your-inquiry">Your inquiry</a><a href="#saved-drafts">Saved drafts</a><a href="#external-services">External services</a><a href="#site-information">Site information</a><a href="#privacy-contact">Contact</a></nav><div class="ut-policy-body">
 <section id="your-inquiry" data-core-section="your-inquiry"><h2>Your inquiry</h2><p>The <a href="/quote/">inquiry form</a> creates an email draft in your browser. It does not send your information to LZZ or upload drawings. To contact us, open the draft in your email app, add your attachments and send it yourself.</p></section>
 <section id="saved-drafts" data-core-section="saved-drafts"><h2>Saved drafts</h2><p>Your input is kept in this browser tab so you can continue after a refresh. The draft is associated with the part or topic used when you entered the form. </p><p>Changing the product or service inside the form updates that same draft; it does not create a separate saved copy. These details are not sent to LZZ or saved to an account.</p><p>Select “Clear saved input” to remove the draft for the current entry context, including older copies associated with that entry. A browser that restores an earlier session may also restore your draft. Clear your input when using a shared device.</p><p>If storage is blocked or full, you can still prepare a draft while the page is open, then choose “Save draft” to keep a text copy.</p></section>
 <section id="external-services" data-core-section="external-services"><h2>Cookies and external services</h2><p>This site does not use analytics or advertising cookies. Your email provider, WhatsApp and other linked websites have their own privacy policies.</p></section>
 <section id="site-information" data-core-section="site-information"><h2>Product and company information</h2><p>Product pages illustrate component forms and explain the information needed to quote a similar part. Your controlled drawing and accepted quotation define the material, tolerances, inspection and commercial terms for the order. Keep order specifications and acceptance records with that drawing revision.</p><p>Use the engineering guides to prepare drawings, material requirements and inspection questions. Agree application-specific validation for the order. Request current <a href="/about/company-profile/#documents">company documents</a> for supplier qualification and include the required records in your <a href="/factory/#quality">inspection plan</a>.</p></section>
 <section id="privacy-contact" data-core-section="privacy-contact"><h2>Contact</h2><p>Hangzhou Lizhizao Precision Machinery Co., Ltd. For questions about this site, contact <a class="contact-link" href="mailto:roger@lzz-cnc.com"><ContactIcon kind="email"/><span>roger@lzz-cnc.com</span></a></p><p class="ut-revision">Updated 18 October 2026.</p></section>
 </div></div></article>
</Layout>

